# L §4.2: day_of(m, n) is "day n of month m ...". Of a key of an anchored index it is refused, at load where load sees
# the index (round 18 C1-15: L4_2_day_of_anchored_load), so here only pm, whose months are calendar months: day 3.
# (Writer 6: was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §4.2 for an anchored month. Writer 8, sixth pass: q1 and q2, over cy and am, moved
# to L4_2_day_of_anchored_load.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input dom: int
index cy = year 2025..2026 from 02-01
index am = month 2026-01..2026-02 from 15
index pm = month 2026-01..2026-02

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  dom = 3 "s"

ask q3: day_of(m, dom) for m in pm
=== expect
q3 (m = 2026-01): 2026-01-03
  cut 2026-12-31
q3 (m = 2026-02): 2026-02-03
  cut 2026-12-31
